### =====================================================================
### Beytak API — manual test suite
###
### SETUP  (do this first, it takes 30 seconds)
###   1. Start the API on the https profile (port 7137).
###   2. Run A2. Copy the "token" value from the response.
###      Paste it below as @userToken.
###   3. Run A3. Copy that token. Paste it below as @adminToken.
###   4. Run C1. Note the "id" in the response.
###      Paste it below as @newHouseId.
###   5. Now run any request. Each one states the status it should return.
###
### Tokens expire after 120 minutes — repeat steps 2 and 3 if you start
### getting 401s on requests that worked before.
### =====================================================================

@host = https://localhost:7137
@api = {{host}}/api

### ---- PASTE VALUES HERE ------------------------------------------------
@userToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..m_xmXOZr4tg3fApK5woZhw8rUIDgxYYYTYqzIm6U5aU
@adminToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..G6S7vGCTCFEk7NtnEWGViyVdn3HnQTur9QtZTQSx3Ac
@newHouseId = 1
@pendingHouseId = 2

### ---- BOOKINGS (section F) ------------------------------------------
@ownerToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..KVkzxe2GqWPQ5A7ZKJ9wB2W1Pir7cTqkefvfVNJR4V4
@strangerToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..IB7hoG4ti3ufcKF-1pHrXrdomfPmOAtCocM_385oO90
@bookingId = 5
@booking2Id = 2
@booking3Id =
@approvedHouseId = 1
@approvedHouse2Id = 5
@pendingListingId = 3
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------


### =====================================================================
### A. AUTHENTICATION
### =====================================================================

### A1 · Register a new account → 200 with a token.
### Change the email each time you run it, or it returns 400.
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test Renter",
  "email": "renter01@test.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0791234567",
  "password": "Test123!"
}

### A2 · Log in as User → 200. COPY THE TOKEN INTO @userToken ABOVE.
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dawud@test.com",
  "password": "Test123!"
}

### A3 · Log in as Admin → 200. COPY THE TOKEN INTO @adminToken ABOVE.
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@beytak.com",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### A4 · Wrong password → 401 "Invalid Email or Password."
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dawud@test.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword1!"
}

### A5 · Unknown email → 401 with the SAME message as A4.
### Identical wording is deliberate: a different message would let an
### attacker discover which emails have accounts.
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@nowhere.com",
  "password": "Test123!"
}

### A6 · Duplicate email → 400 "Email is already registered."
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Duplicate User",
  "email": "dawud@test.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0790000000",
  "password": "Test123!"
}

### A7 · Weak password → 400 listing Identity's own rules
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Weak Password",
  "email": "weak01@test.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0790000000",
  "password": "abcdef"
}

### A8 · Invalid model → 400 with field-level errors
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "phoneNumber": "0790000000",
  "password": "abc"
}


### =====================================================================
### B. LISTINGS — PUBLIC (no token needed)
### =====================================================================

### B1 · Search with no filters → 200, approved + available only
GET {{api}}/houses

### B2 · Filter by city → 200
GET {{api}}/houses?city=Amman

### B3 · City with no matches → 200 and an empty array, not a 404
GET {{api}}/houses?city=Zarqa

### B4 · Minimum bedrooms — asking for 2 also returns 3-bed listings
GET {{api}}/houses?bedrooms=2

### B5 · More bedrooms than any listing has → empty
GET {{api}}/houses?bedrooms=10

### B6 · Price range
GET {{api}}/houses?minPrice=100&maxPrice=800

### B7 · Price floor above every listing → empty
GET {{api}}/houses?minPrice=99999

### B8 · Furnished only
GET {{api}}/houses?isFurnished=true

### B9 · Property type — 1 Apartment · 2 House · 3 Villa · 4 Studio · 5 Room
GET {{api}}/houses?propertyType=1

### B10 · Rental period — 1 Weekly · 2 Monthly · 3 Yearly
GET {{api}}/houses?priceUnit=2

### B11 · Several filters at once, resolved in a single SQL query
GET {{api}}/houses?city=Amman&propertyType=1&bedrooms=2&isFurnished=true&maxPrice=800

### B12 · SECURITY — a stranger asking for pending listings.
### HouseService overwrites Status with Approved, so this returns
### approved listings only. Nothing Pending may appear here.
GET {{api}}/houses?status=Pending

### B13 · Invalid enum in a filter → 400
GET {{api}}/houses?propertyType=99

### B14 · Detail of an approved listing → 200
GET {{api}}/houses/{{newHouseId}}

### B15 · Listing that does not exist → 404
GET {{api}}/houses/9999

### B16 · SECURITY — detail of a PENDING listing as a stranger → 404
GET {{api}}/houses/{{pendingHouseId}}

### B17 · Non-numeric id → 404, not a 500.
### The {id:int} route constraint is what makes "mine" and "pending"
### reach their own actions instead of being parsed as an id.
GET {{api}}/houses/abc


### =====================================================================
### C. LISTINGS — OWNER (needs @userToken)
### =====================================================================

### C1 · Create a listing → 201, status "Pending", Location header set.
### COPY THE "id" FROM THE RESPONSE INTO @newHouseId ABOVE.
### Note there is no ownerId in the body — it comes from the token.
POST {{api}}/houses
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Renovated 2-bedroom in Jabal Al Weibdeh",
  "description": "Quiet street close to cafes and the cultural centre. Recently renovated with new kitchen and bathroom fittings.",
  "propertyType": 1,
  "address": "Jabal Al Weibdeh, Building 4",
  "city": "Amman",
  "neighborhood": "Jabal Al Weibdeh",
  "price": 400,
  "priceUnit": 2,
  "bedrooms": 2,
  "bathrooms": 1,
  "areaSqM": 110,
  "isFurnished": false,
  "floorNumber": 2,
  "masterBedrooms": 1,
  "apartmentsInBuilding": 6,
  "buildingAge": 3,
  "turnoverDays": 2,
  "imageUrls": ["/uploads/houses/weibdeh-1.jpg", "/uploads/houses/weibdeh-2.jpg"]
}

### C2 · The owner CAN see their own pending listing → 200
GET {{api}}/houses/{{newHouseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### C3 · A stranger CANNOT see the same listing → 404
GET {{api}}/houses/{{newHouseId}}

### C4 · The owner's listings → 200, every status, newest first
GET {{api}}/houses/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### C5 · Create without a token → 401
POST {{api}}/houses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Unauthorised listing",
  "description": "This must never be created because no token was sent.",
  "propertyType": 1,
  "address": "Nowhere",
  "city": "Amman",
  "price": 300,
  "priceUnit": 2,
  "bedrooms": 1,
  "bathrooms": 1,
  "areaSqM": 50
}

### C6 · Validation — empty title and a price of zero → 400
POST {{api}}/houses
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "An empty title and a zero price should both fail validation.",
  "propertyType": 1,
  "address": "Somewhere",
  "city": "Amman",
  "price": 0,
  "priceUnit": 2,
  "bedrooms": 1,
  "bathrooms": 1,
  "areaSqM": 50
}

### C7 · SECURITY — the client tries to set ownerId and status itself.
### Neither field exists on HouseCreateDto, so both are discarded.
### The response must show YOUR user id and status "Pending".
POST {{api}}/houses
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Attempted ownership and status override",
  "description": "The ownerId and status values below must be ignored by the API.",
  "propertyType": 1,
  "address": "Test Street",
  "city": "Amman",
  "price": 300,
  "priceUnit": 2,
  "bedrooms": 1,
  "bathrooms": 1,
  "areaSqM": 50,
  "ownerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "status": 2
}

### C8 · Undefined enum value → 400.
### C# enums are integers, so 99 deserializes happily. Only the
### [EnumDataType] attribute on HouseCreateDto rejects it.
POST {{api}}/houses
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Invalid property type",
  "description": "PropertyType 99 is not a defined member of the enum.",
  "propertyType": 99,
  "address": "Test Street",
  "city": "Amman",
  "price": 300,
  "priceUnit": 2,
  "bedrooms": 1,
  "bathrooms": 1,
  "areaSqM": 50
}


### =====================================================================
### D. LISTINGS — ADMIN (needs @adminToken)
### =====================================================================

### D1 · Review queue → 200, pending listings only
GET {{api}}/houses/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### D2 · An admin can see any listing whatever its status → 200
GET {{api}}/houses/{{newHouseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### D3 · Approve → 200, status becomes "Approved"
PATCH {{api}}/houses/{{newHouseId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### D4 · Now visible to everyone → 200
GET {{api}}/houses/{{newHouseId}}

### D5 · Approving twice → 400 "This listing is already approved."
PATCH {{api}}/houses/{{newHouseId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### D6 · Reject a listing → 200, status becomes "Rejected"
PATCH {{api}}/houses/{{pendingHouseId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### D7 · A rejected listing is gone from public search
GET {{api}}/houses

### D8 · Approve something that does not exist → 400 "Listing not found."
PATCH {{api}}/houses/9999/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### =====================================================================
### E. AUTHORIZATION BOUNDARIES
### =====================================================================

### E1 · Review queue with no token → 401 (not authenticated)
GET {{api}}/houses/pending

### E2 · Review queue with a USER token → 403 (authenticated, wrong role)
GET {{api}}/houses/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### E3 · Approve with a USER token → 403
PATCH {{api}}/houses/{{newHouseId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### E4 · Owner's listings with no token → 401
GET {{api}}/houses/mine

### E5 · Malformed token → 401
GET {{api}}/houses/mine
Authorization: Bearer not.a.real.token


### =====================================================================
### F. BOOKINGS
###
### SETUP for this section (order matters — run F0a to F0d first):
###   @userToken     must be the RENTER   -> renter01@test.com
###   @ownerToken    must be the OWNER    -> dawud@test.com
###   @strangerToken must be a THIRD user -> renter02@test.com
###
### House 1 is Approved, 550 JOD Monthly, TurnoverDays = 2, owned by dawud.
### House 5 is Approved, 400 JOD Monthly, TurnoverDays = 2, owned by dawud.
### House 3 is Pending.
###
### Run F1, F6 and F25 in order and paste the booking ids above as you go.
### =====================================================================

### F0a · Log in as the RENTER -> 200. COPY TOKEN INTO @userToken.
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "renter01@test.com",
  "password": "Test123!"
}

### F0b · Log in as the OWNER -> 200. COPY TOKEN INTO @ownerToken.
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dawud@test.com",
  "password": "Test123!"
}

### F0c · Register a THIRD user -> 200. COPY TOKEN INTO @strangerToken.
### If it returns 400 the account already exists - use F0d instead.
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Nosy Stranger",
  "email": "renter03@test.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0799999999",
  "password": "Test123!"
}

### F0d · Log in as the third user -> 200. COPY TOKEN INTO @strangerToken.
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "renter03@test.com",
  "password": "Test123!"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### F1-F3 · HAPPY PATH
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### F1 · Create a booking -> 201 Created, with a Location header.
### Expect: status "Pending", totalPrice 550.00 (550 x 1),
###         startDate 2026-10-01, endDate 2026-11-01, lastNight 2026-10-31,
###         ownerPhone null and renterPhone null (not confirmed yet).
### COPY THE "id" INTO @bookingId ABOVE.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2026-10-01",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F2 · Read it back as the renter -> 200.
### Expect ownerPhone null, because the booking is still Pending.
GET {{api}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### F3 · The renter's own bookings -> 200, array containing F1.
GET {{api}}/bookings/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### F4-F7 · OVERLAP AND THE TURNOVER GAP  (House 1, TurnoverDays = 2)
###
### F1 occupies 2026-10-01 -> 2026-11-01 (end exclusive).
### With a 2-day gap, the next booking may not start before 2026-11-03.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### F4 · Exactly the same dates -> 400 "Those dates are not available."
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2026-10-01",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F5 · Starts 2026-11-02 - only ONE free day -> 400.
### This is the turnover rule. Without the padding this would wrongly return 201.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2026-11-02",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F6 · Starts 2026-11-03 - exactly TWO free days -> 201.
### COPY THE "id" INTO @booking2Id ABOVE.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2026-11-03",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F7 · Overlaps F1 from BEFORE (2026-09-20 -> 2026-10-20) -> 400.
### Proves the padding applies on both sides, not only after.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2026-09-20",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 2
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### F8-F12 · BUSINESS RULES
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### F8 · The owner books their own property -> 400 "You cannot book your own property."
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2027-01-05",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F9 · Book a Pending (unapproved) listing -> 400 "not available for booking."
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": {{pendingListingId}},
  "startDate": "2027-01-05",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F10 · Weekly booking on a Monthly-priced house -> 400 "rented Monthly only."
### Without this check the total would be three months' rent for three weeks.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2027-01-05",
  "durationCount": 3,
  "durationType": 1
}

### F11 · Start date in the past -> 400 "Start date cannot be in the past."
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2020-01-01",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F12 · Unknown house -> 400 "Property not found."
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 9999,
  "startDate": "2027-01-05",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 2
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### F13-F15 · INPUT VALIDATION  (400 from the model binder, before the service)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### F13 · durationCount 0 -> 400, "DurationCount" listed in the errors object.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2027-01-05",
  "durationCount": 0,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F14 · durationCount 99, above the max of 60 -> 400.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2027-01-05",
  "durationCount": 99,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F15 · durationType 99, not a defined enum value -> 400.
### C# enums are ints, so without [EnumDataType] this would be accepted.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2027-01-05",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 99
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### F16-F19 · WHO CAN SEE A BOOKING
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### F16 · A stranger reads someone else's booking -> 404, not 403.
### 404 hides whether the booking exists at all.
GET {{api}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{strangerToken}}

### F17 · The house owner reads it -> 200.
GET {{api}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### F18 · An admin reads it -> 200.
GET {{api}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### F19 · The owner's incoming requests -> 200, contains F1 and F6.
### Expect renterPhone null on every Pending row.
GET {{api}}/bookings/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### F20-F24 · STATUS TRANSITIONS
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### F20 · The RENTER tries to confirm -> 400 "You do not own this property."
PATCH {{api}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### F21 · The OWNER confirms -> 200.
### Expect status "Confirmed" AND ownerPhone + renterPhone now populated.
### This is the contact gate opening.
PATCH {{api}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### F22 · Confirm the same booking again -> 400 "already Confirmed."
PATCH {{api}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### F23 · The renter cancels a CONFIRMED booking -> 400 "already Confirmed."
### Change this expectation if you decide renters may cancel after confirmation.
PATCH {{api}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### F24 · The owner rejects the second booking -> 200, status "Rejected".
### Expect the phone fields back to null.
PATCH {{api}}/bookings/{{booking2Id}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### F25-F27 · CANCEL PATH
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### F25 · Create a booking on House 5 -> 201. COPY THE "id" INTO @booking3Id.
### Expect totalPrice 800.00 (400 x 2).
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": {{approvedHouse2Id}},
  "startDate": "2026-12-01",
  "durationCount": 2,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F26 · The renter cancels it -> 200, status "Cancelled".
PATCH {{api}}/bookings/{{booking3Id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### F27 · The dates freed by F26 are bookable again -> 201.
### Cancelled bookings must not keep holding the calendar.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{strangerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": {{approvedHouse2Id}},
  "startDate": "2026-12-01",
  "durationCount": 2,
  "durationType": 2
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### F28-F30 · AUTHORIZATION BOUNDARIES
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### F28 · Create with no token -> 401.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "houseId": 1,
  "startDate": "2027-01-05",
  "durationCount": 1,
  "durationType": 2
}

### F29 · My bookings with no token -> 401.
GET {{api}}/bookings/mine

### F30 · A user with no bookings -> 200 and an empty array, not 404.
GET {{api}}/bookings/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
